module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.bare_name_resolved_by_proximity_standing_in_for_resolution

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data bare_name_resolved_by_proximity_standing_in_for_resolution: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "bare_name_resolved_by_proximity_standing_in_for_resolution" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**bare name resolved by proximity, standing in for resolution** (the reference-edge reader in `v1_compiler.cli_run` `entry_resolve` binds a bare name in an IMPORT-LESS file by 'proximity disambiguation' -- the longest shared module-path prefix with a pool declarer -- yielding a UniqueBare or AmbiguousBare edge. A heuristic standing where lexical resolution (locals plus imports) is the authority; DESIGN §4: in a closed system a heuristic is never necessary.)",

    "INVALID STATE: a dependency edge from a module to a declarer it does not lexically bind. The edge widens closures and affected-set selection and can name a homonym the source never meant, silently, with no refusal.",

    "SPECIMEN (gunbc#13526, open when this row was written): a supplied fixture declaring a homonym `Present` beside `std.optional { Present }` produced an edge from an importer of `std.optional` to the homonym's module while the reader still resolved by proximity. #13526 closed the arm for import-BEARING files (bare names there are lexically bound, only qualified chains become edges) and kept the proximity tier for import-less files only.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT (gunbc#13533): silent wrongness on the import-less UniqueBare path, outside the ladder. Import-bearing files were already closed by #13526.",

    "EVIDENCE, EXECUTED: the import-less wrong-edge RED is `cli_run` `reference_edge_producer_tests` `proximity_must_not_bind_an_importless_bare_name_to_a_sibling_homonym`, over the real `dependency_resolution_facts` union (not a mutant). Fixture: `frontier.child.consumer` calls `duplicated()`; `frontier` and `frontier.child.plant` both declare it. On main before the climb, UniqueBare was `[frontier.child.plant]` (ctrl-build --remote cargo test --release -p v1-compiler --lib proximity_must_not_bind_an_importless_bare_name_to_a_sibling_homonym: assertion `proximity UniqueBare bound the sibling plant`, 0 passed / 1 failed, 0.00s). After the climb the same test is the permanent regression control: no plant edge, UniqueBare to the on-chain ancestor `frontier`. Positive control: `an_importless_bare_name_on_the_ancestor_chain_still_resolves`. Inhabitance: `load_sources_binds_the_on_chain_ancestor_not_the_sibling_plant`. The former proximity-live control `the_same_bare_name_without_the_import_still_resolves` is now `the_same_bare_name_without_the_import_does_not_proximity_bind`.",

    "RUNG NOW: structurally guaranteed on the UniqueBare producer (source -> accepted graph). UniqueBare is the unique on-chain declarer (`global_bare_chain_candidates` predicate); two or more on-chain are AmbiguousBare; zero on-chain is not an edge -- no nearest-prefix rank, no superset fallback. The proximity loop is deleted from `reference_edges_for_file` and from `reference_targets_of`. CEILING 3. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: none on this producer. Off-chain unique names still UniqueBinding-pulled by the compile-closure census are a different class (`binding_chosen_by_pool_membership_rather_than_by_the_declared_rule` / UniqueBinding), not this ranking.",

    "REVIEW TELL: a reader or resolver that ranks candidate declarers by path similarity, shared prefix or 'closest' instead of refusing; an edge whose only justification is that one pool declarer exists.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
